      <h2>Systems we install</h2>

      <h3>TPO (thermoplastic polyolefin)</h3>
      <p>The most common commercial roofing material in the Springs. White reflective membrane, 60-mil standard, 20&ndash;30 year life. Great for warehouses, retail, and any flat or low-slope roof. We heat-weld every seam; mechanically-fastened is available but we prefer fully-adhered for wind-prone locations above 6,500 ft.</p>

      <h3>EPDM (rubber)</h3>
      <p>Black synthetic rubber, very durable, 40-year proven track record. Best for buildings that don't need reflective properties and where the budget-to-lifespan ratio is paramount. We install in full sheets up to 50'&times;100' to minimize seams.</p>

      <h3>PVC</h3>
      <p>Similar to TPO but with chemical resistance &mdash; the right call for restaurants (grease exhaust), hospitals (disinfectants), or anywhere an industrial process might reach the roof. Heat-welded seams, 30-year typical life.</p>

      <h3>Modified bitumen</h3>
      <p>Two-ply or three-ply asphalt-based system with a granulated cap sheet. Still the right answer on older buildings with built-up roof systems. We torch-down in accordance with fire codes and NFPA standards.</p>

      <h3>Standing-seam metal</h3>
      <p>For pitched commercial roofs and premium projects. 40&ndash;60 year life. Higher install cost, but you won't replace it in your operational lifetime.</p>

      <h2>How we work with building owners and property managers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Phased installation.</strong> We section the roof into zones and install during business hours when possible, after-hours when not.</li>
        <li><strong>Daily clean-up.</strong> No debris sitting in your parking lot overnight. No blocked fire lanes. No tenant complaints about trash at the dumpster enclosure.</li>
        <li><strong>Coordination with HVAC.</strong> We work with your HVAC contractor on curb-mounted units, reseating them on new flashing and insulation without damaging connections.</li>
        <li><strong>Tenant notice.</strong> We'll draft the tenant-notification email if you'd like &mdash; covers schedule, expected noise, access, and whom to call if there's an issue.</li>
        <li><strong>Weekly progress reports.</strong> Photos, completed square footage, upcoming phase. One email per week. You're never guessing where we are.</li>
        <li><strong>Permit &amp; inspection handling.</strong> We pull permits, coordinate with Colorado Springs building department, and meet inspectors. You just sign the completion certificate.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Bonding and insurance</h2>
      <p>For commercial work we carry:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>$5M</strong> commercial general liability</li>
        <li><strong>$1M</strong> auto liability</li>
        <li><strong>Colorado workers' comp</strong> (mandatory, but we mention it because some competitors aren't fully covered)</li>
        <li><strong>Performance and payment bonds</strong> up to $2M per project available</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We provide certificates of insurance naming your LLC or management company as additional insured before any crew arrives on-site. This is table stakes for commercial work &mdash; ask every bidder for the same.</p>

      <h2>What a typical commercial re-roof looks like</h2>
      <p>For a 20,000 sq ft single-story commercial building on TPO:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Week 1:</strong> Site setup, crane positioning (if needed), deck inspection, insulation removal in the first zone.</li>
        <li><strong>Weeks 2&ndash;3:</strong> New insulation, cover board, TPO membrane, all flashing, penetrations, and curbs in the first half of the building.</li>
        <li><strong>Weeks 4&ndash;5:</strong> Second half. Final walkaround with the building manager.</li>
        <li><strong>Day 28&ndash;35:</strong> Punch list, warranty paperwork, final inspection.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Larger buildings (50,000&ndash;100,000 sq ft) scale roughly linearly. We provide a Gantt-style schedule with the estimate so you can plan tenant communications.</p>
